{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RN6zYBVEG2xFCiE2LQG86g","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Coverage Gap Report\n2\t\n3\t**Library:** PathFinding.js  \n4\t**Test suite:** `npx mocha --require should test/**/*.js`  \n5\t**Result:** 57 passing, 0 failing  \n6\t**Date:** 2026-04-16\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## Summary\n11\t\n12\tAll finders pass 4 scenario-based maze tests each. Core utilities have basic happy-path tests. No edge-case, no-path, constructor option, or diagonal-variant coverage exists for most finders. Two finders are entirely untested. One utility function (`smoothenPath`) is completely absent from tests.\n13\t\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## src/core/Node.js\n17\t\n18\t**What IS tested:** Implicitly exercised by every finder test (nodes created via Grid).\n19\t\n20\t**What is NOT tested:**\n21\t- Direct construction: `new Node(x, y)` — default `walkable=true` branch\n22\t- Explicit `walkable=false` constructor arg\n23\t- No unit tests for Node in isolation\n24\t\n25\t**Priority:** Low — trivial constructor, but a dedicated unit test would catch regressions.\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## src/core/DiagonalMovement.js\n30\t\n31\t**What IS tested:** Values referenced indirectly by Grid/finder tests.\n32\t\n33\t**What is NOT tested:**\n34\t- No test verifies the enum values (`Always=1`, `Never=2`, `IfAtMostOneObstacle=3`, `OnlyWhenNoObstacles=4`) are stable/correct\n35\t- Invalid value passed to `Grid.getNeighbors` → should throw `'Incorrect value of diagonalMovement'` (branch at Grid.js:195) — **untested**\n36\t\n37\t**Priority:** Medium — the error-throw branch in `Grid.getNeighbors` is a real code path that is never exercised.\n38\t\n39\t---\n40\t\n41\t## src/core/Grid.js\n42\t\n43\t**What IS tested:**\n44\t- Constructor with `(width, height)` — no matrix\n45\t- Constructor with `(matrix)` — no width/height\n46\t- Constructor with `(width, height, matrix)`\n47\t- `isWalkableAt`, `setWalkableAt`, `isInside`\n48\t- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Never` and `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle`\n49\t\n50\t**What is NOT tested:**\n51\t- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Always` — `d0=d1=d2=d3=true` branch (Grid.js:189)\n52\t- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` — `d = s3 && s0` branch (Grid.js:180)\n53\t- `getNeighbors` with invalid `diagonalMovement` → should `throw new Error('Incorrect value of diagonalMovement')` (Grid.js:195)\n54\t- `_buildNodes` with mismatched matrix dimensions → should throw `'Matrix size does not fit'` (Grid.js:66)\n55\t- `clone()` — never called in any test; cloned walkability not verified\n56\t- `getNodeAt` — not tested directly (used internally only)\n57\t- Corner node neighbor pruning (nodes at grid edges where diagonal would be out-of-bounds)\n58\t\n59\t**Priority:** High — `clone()` is used by finders internally but untested directly; matrix-mismatch and invalid diagonal-movement errors are completely uncovered.\n60\t\n61\t---\n62\t\n63\t## src/core/Heuristic.js\n64\t\n65\t**What IS tested:** Nothing directly. Functions used implicitly by finders.\n66\t\n67\t**What is NOT tested:**\n68\t- `manhattan(dx, dy)` — e.g. `manhattan(3, 4)` should return `7`\n69\t- `euclidean(dx, dy)` — e.g. `euclidean(3, 4)` should return `5`\n70\t- `octile(dx, dy)` — both `dx < dy` and `dx >= dy` branches\n71\t- `chebyshev(dx, dy)` — e.g. `chebyshev(3, 4)` should return `4`\n72\t- Zero inputs: all four functions with `(0, 0)` → should return `0`\n73\t- Symmetry: `heuristic(a, b) === heuristic(b, a)` for octile/chebyshev\n74\t\n75\t**Priority:** High — pure functions, trivial to unit test, but zero coverage. Bugs here silently corrupt all heuristic-based finders.\n76\t\n77\t---\n78\t\n79\t## src/core/Util.js\n80\t\n81\t**What IS tested:**\n82\t- `interpolate(0, 1, 0, 4)` — vertical line only\n83\t- `expandPath([])` — empty input\n84\t- `expandPath([[0,1],[0,4]])` — two-segment path\n85\t- `expandPath([[0,1],[0,4],[2,6]])` — three-segment path\n86\t- `compressPath([])` — empty path (< 3 nodes, returns as-is)\n87\t- `compressPath` — straight vertical then diagonal\n88\t\n89\t**What is NOT tested:**\n90\t- `interpolate` — horizontal line (`x0 != x1, y0 == y1`)\n91\t- `interpolate` — diagonal line\n92\t- `interpolate` — same start/end point (`x0==x1, y0==y1`) → single-element result\n93\t- `backtrace` — no direct test; only exercised indirectly\n94\t- `biBacktrace` — no direct test\n95\t- `pathLength` — entirely untested; zero coverage\n96\t- `smoothenPath` — entirely untested; the function also contains a **bug**: `lastValidCoord` is used without declaration (implicit global) at Util.js:167\n97\t- `compressPath` with single-element path (length = 1) — boundary: returns path as-is\n98\t- `compressPath` with two-element path (length = 2) — boundary\n99\t\n100\t**Priority:** High — `smoothenPath` has zero coverage AND contains an undeclared variable bug (`lastValidCoord` at line 167). `pathLength` and `biBacktrace` are completely untested.\n101\t\n102\t---\n103\t\n104\t## src/finders/AStarFinder.js\n105\t\n106\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios with default constructor (`DiagonalMovement.Never`, `manhattan` heuristic).\n107\t\n108\t**What is NOT tested:**\n109\t- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` + `octile`\n110\t- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true, dontCrossCorners: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles`\n111\t- Constructor with explicit `diagonalMovement` option (all four values)\n112\t- Constructor with custom `heuristic` function\n113\t- Constructor with `weight` != 1 (weighted A*)\n114\t- No-path scenario (start/end isolated by walls) → should return `[]`\n115\t- Start == End (same node) → should return `[[x,y]]` or `[]` — behavior unspecified/untested\n116\t- `findPath` — neighbor already in open list with better g-score (the `openList.updateItem` branch at AStarFinder.js:116)\n117\t\n118\t**Priority:** High — the `weight`, custom heuristic, and no-path scenarios are critical behavioral paths with zero coverage.\n119\t\n120\t---\n121\t\n122\t## src/finders/DijkstraFinder.js\n123\t\n124\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (inherits AStarFinder with `heuristic = 0`).\n125\t\n126\t**What is NOT tested:** Same gaps as AStarFinder. Additionally:\n127\t- Verify heuristic override to `0` — distances should reflect true uniform cost\n128\t\n129\t**Priority:** Medium.\n130\t\n131\t---\n132\t\n133\t## src/finders/BestFirstFinder.js\n134\t\n135\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal check only: start/end coords).\n136\t\n137\t**What is NOT tested:**\n138\t- Custom heuristic injection\n139\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n140\t- Constructor option coverage (same as AStarFinder)\n141\t- The `* 1000000` scaling effect: on an open grid, path should be greedy (go straight to goal)\n142\t\n143\t**Priority:** Medium.\n144\t\n145\t---\n146\t\n147\t## src/finders/BreadthFirstFinder.js\n148\t\n149\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios with default options.\n150\t\n151\t**What is NOT tested:**\n152\t- Diagonal movement enabled variants\n153\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n154\t- Start == End\n155\t- Constructor `allowDiagonal` / `dontCrossCorners` / `diagonalMovement` options\n156\t\n157\t**Priority:** Medium.\n158\t\n159\t---\n160\t\n161\t## src/finders/BiAStarFinder.js\n162\t\n163\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal check only).\n164\t\n165\t**What is NOT tested:**\n166\t- All constructor options (same as AStarFinder)\n167\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n168\t- The `biBacktrace(node, neighbor)` meeting-point path join — only implicitly hit\n169\t- The `biBacktrace(neighbor, node)` reverse direction join (end-side expansion finds start-side node)\n170\t- Both expansion directions (start-side and end-side) meeting\n171\t\n172\t**Priority:** High — bi-directional meeting logic is complex and the two `biBacktrace` call sites are never explicitly asserted.\n173\t\n174\t---\n175\t\n176\t## src/finders/BiBreadthFirstFinder.js\n177\t\n178\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (optimal check).\n179\t\n180\t**What is NOT tested:**\n181\t- Diagonal movement variants\n182\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n183\t- `biBacktrace` call from end-side expansion (BiBreadthFirstFinder.js:100)\n184\t- Start == End\n185\t\n186\t**Priority:** Medium.\n187\t\n188\t---\n189\t\n190\t## src/finders/BiDijkstraFinder.js\n191\t\n192\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (optimal).\n193\t\n194\t**What is NOT tested:** Same gaps as BiAStarFinder + DijkstraFinder.\n195\t\n196\t**Priority:** Medium.\n197\t\n198\t---\n199\t\n200\t## src/finders/BiBestFirstFinder.js\n201\t\n202\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal).\n203\t\n204\t**What is NOT tested:** Same gaps as BestFirstFinder + bi-directional meeting logic.\n205\t\n206\t**Priority:** Medium.\n207\t\n208\t---\n209\t\n210\t## src/finders/IDAStarFinder.js\n211\t\n212\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal check only).\n213\t\n214\t**What is NOT tested:**\n215\t- `trackRecursion: true` — `retainCount` and `tested` tracking branches (IDAStarFinder.js:137-144)\n216\t- `timeLimit` option — path not found due to time expiry → `[]` (IDAStarFinder.js:105-108)\n217\t- `weight` != 1\n218\t- Custom heuristic\n219\t- Diagonal movement variants\n220\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n221\t- The `route` array construction (IDAStarFinder.js:118-121) — only implicitly verified\n222\t\n223\t**Priority:** High — `timeLimit` and `trackRecursion` are unique features with zero test coverage.\n224\t\n225\t---\n226\t\n227\t## src/finders/JumpPointFinder.js (factory)\n228\t\n229\t**What IS tested:**\n230\t- `DiagonalMovement.Never` → `JPFNeverMoveDiagonally`\n231\t- `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` → `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle`\n232\t\n233\t**What is NOT tested:**\n234\t- `DiagonalMovement.Always` → `JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally` — **no tests at all**\n235\t- `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` → `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles` — **no tests at all**\n236\t- Default (no option) → falls through to `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle`\n237\t\n238\t**Priority:** High — two of four factory branches (`Always`, `OnlyWhenNoObstacles`) produce untested finders.\n239\t\n240\t---\n241\t\n242\t## src/finders/JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally.js\n243\t\n244\t**What IS tested:** Nothing — zero test coverage.\n245\t\n246\t**What is NOT tested:**\n247\t- `_jump` — diagonal movement detection of forced neighbors (JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally.js:43-51)\n248\t- `_jump` — horizontal forced neighbor detection (line 56-59)\n249\t- `_jump` — vertical forced neighbor detection (line 61-64)\n250\t- `_jump` — end-node detection\n251\t- `_jump` — out-of-bounds / unwalkable returns null\n252\t- `_findNeighbors` — diagonal parent direction (line 94-110)\n253\t- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal parent direction\n254\t- `_findNeighbors` — vertical parent direction\n255\t- `_findNeighbors` — no parent (returns all neighbors)\n256\t- End-to-end `findPath` — any maze at all\n257\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n258\t- `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n259\t\n260\t**Priority:** High — entire file untested.\n261\t\n262\t---\n263\t\n264\t## src/finders/JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles.js\n265\t\n266\t**What IS tested:** Nothing — zero test coverage.\n267\t\n268\t**What is NOT tested:**\n269\t- `_jump` — commented-out forced-neighbor check at line 44-47 (deliberate omission, but untested)\n270\t- `_jump` — diagonal sub-jump calls (line 49)\n271\t- `_jump` — horizontal forced neighbors (line 56-59)\n272\t- `_jump` — vertical forced neighbors (line 62-65)\n273\t- `_jump` — diagonal continuation gating (`isWalkableAt(x+dx,y) && isWalkableAt(x,y+dy)`) at line 75\n274\t- `_findNeighbors` — all parent-direction branches\n275\t- End-to-end `findPath` — any maze\n276\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n277\t\n278\t**Priority:** High — entire file untested.\n279\t\n280\t---\n281\t\n282\t## src/finders/JPFNeverMoveDiagonally.js\n283\t\n284\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal).\n285\t\n286\t**What is NOT tested:**\n287\t- `_jump` — horizontal direction forced-neighbor detection (line 42-45)\n288\t- `_jump` — vertical direction + recursive horizontal sub-jumps (line 53)\n289\t- `_jump` — `throw new Error(\"Only horizontal and vertical movements are allowed\")` (line 58) — diagonal dx/dy input never tested\n290\t- `_jump` — `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n291\t- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal parent direction\n292\t- `_findNeighbors` — vertical parent direction\n293\t- `_findNeighbors` — no parent\n294\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n295\t\n296\t**Priority:** High — error-throw branch and recursion path in `_jump` uncovered.\n297\t\n298\t---\n299\t\n300\t## src/finders/JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle.js\n301\t\n302\t**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal).\n303\t\n304\t**What is NOT tested:**\n305\t- `_jump` — diagonal forced-neighbor detection branches (line 43-47)\n306\t- `_jump` — diagonal continuation gating (`isWalkableAt(x+dx,y) || isWalkableAt(x,y+dy)`) at line 71 — the `null` return branch when both blocked\n307\t- `_jump` — `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n308\t- `_findNeighbors` — diagonal parent: forced neighbor additions at lines 110-115\n309\t- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal parent: forced-obstacle-adjacent diagonal neighbors\n310\t- `_findNeighbors` — no parent\n311\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n312\t\n313\t**Priority:** High — diagonal continuation null-return branch and forced-neighbor pruning logic untested.\n314\t\n315\t---\n316\t\n317\t## src/finders/JumpPointFinderBase.js\n318\t\n319\t**What IS tested:** `findPath` loop runs via all JPF subclass tests.\n320\t\n321\t**What is NOT tested:**\n322\t- `_identifySuccessors` — `jumpNode.closed` skip branch (line 89)\n323\t- `_identifySuccessors` — `openList.updateItem` branch (ng < jumpNode.g, line 107)\n324\t- `trackJumpRecursion: true` option (base class stores flag but never tested at base level)\n325\t- No-path scenario (open list exhausted) → `[]`\n326\t\n327\t**Priority:** Medium.\n328\t\n329\t---\n330\t\n331\t## Cross-cutting gaps\n332\t\n333\t| Gap | Affected finders | Priority |\n334\t|-----|-----------------|----------|\n335\t| No-path (isolated start or end) returns `[]` | All 11 finders | **High** |\n336\t| Start == End returns path | All finders | Medium |\n337\t| `DiagonalMovement.Always` end-to-end | JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally | **High** |\n338\t| `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` end-to-end | JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles | **High** |\n339\t| `smoothenPath` — zero coverage + bug (undeclared `lastValidCoord`) | Util.js:167 | **High** |\n340\t| `pathLength` — zero coverage | Util.js | **High** |\n341\t| Heuristic unit tests | Heuristic.js | **High** |\n342\t| `Grid.clone()` — zero direct coverage | Grid.js | High |\n343\t| Matrix dimension mismatch error | Grid.js | Medium |\n344\t| `IDAStarFinder` timeLimit expiry | IDAStarFinder.js | High |\n345\t| `IDAStarFinder` trackRecursion | IDAStarFinder.js | Medium |\n346\t| Deprecated `allowDiagonal` / `dontCrossCorners` options | AStarFinder, BFS, Dijkstra, … | Low |\n347\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72a8c5be-b7cd-4258-8cfe-39ab16c21233","uuid":"b745e2ac-dbf6-46c4-a203-50936b115253","timestamp":"2026-04-16T13:59:08.626Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/coverage-auditor/output/gap-report.md","content":"# Test Coverage Gap Report\n\n**Library:** PathFinding.js  \n**Test suite:** `npx mocha --require should test/**/*.js`  \n**Result:** 57 passing, 0 failing  \n**Date:** 2026-04-16\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nAll finders pass 4 scenario-based maze tests each. Core utilities have basic happy-path tests. No edge-case, no-path, constructor option, or diagonal-variant coverage exists for most finders. Two finders are entirely untested. One utility function (`smoothenPath`) is completely absent from tests.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Node.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Implicitly exercised by every finder test (nodes created via Grid).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- Direct construction: `new Node(x, y)` — default `walkable=true` branch\n- Explicit `walkable=false` constructor arg\n- No unit tests for Node in isolation\n\n**Priority:** Low — trivial constructor, but a dedicated unit test would catch regressions.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/DiagonalMovement.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Values referenced indirectly by Grid/finder tests.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- No test verifies the enum values (`Always=1`, `Never=2`, `IfAtMostOneObstacle=3`, `OnlyWhenNoObstacles=4`) are stable/correct\n- Invalid value passed to `Grid.getNeighbors` → should throw `'Incorrect value of diagonalMovement'` (branch at Grid.js:195) — **untested**\n\n**Priority:** Medium — the error-throw branch in `Grid.getNeighbors` is a real code path that is never exercised.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Grid.js\n\n**What IS tested:**\n- Constructor with `(width, height)` — no matrix\n- Constructor with `(matrix)` — no width/height\n- Constructor with `(width, height, matrix)`\n- `isWalkableAt`, `setWalkableAt`, `isInside`\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Never` and `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle`\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Always` — `d0=d1=d2=d3=true` branch (Grid.js:189)\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` — `d = s3 && s0` branch (Grid.js:180)\n- `getNeighbors` with invalid `diagonalMovement` → should `throw new Error('Incorrect value of diagonalMovement')` (Grid.js:195)\n- `_buildNodes` with mismatched matrix dimensions → should throw `'Matrix size does not fit'` (Grid.js:66)\n- `clone()` — never called in any test; cloned walkability not verified\n- `getNodeAt` — not tested directly (used internally only)\n- Corner node neighbor pruning (nodes at grid edges where diagonal would be out-of-bounds)\n\n**Priority:** High — `clone()` is used by finders internally but untested directly; matrix-mismatch and invalid diagonal-movement errors are completely uncovered.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Heuristic.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Nothing directly. Functions used implicitly by finders.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `manhattan(dx, dy)` — e.g. `manhattan(3, 4)` should return `7`\n- `euclidean(dx, dy)` — e.g. `euclidean(3, 4)` should return `5`\n- `octile(dx, dy)` — both `dx < dy` and `dx >= dy` branches\n- `chebyshev(dx, dy)` — e.g. `chebyshev(3, 4)` should return `4`\n- Zero inputs: all four functions with `(0, 0)` → should return `0`\n- Symmetry: `heuristic(a, b) === heuristic(b, a)` for octile/chebyshev\n\n**Priority:** High — pure functions, trivial to unit test, but zero coverage. Bugs here silently corrupt all heuristic-based finders.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Util.js\n\n**What IS tested:**\n- `interpolate(0, 1, 0, 4)` — vertical line only\n- `expandPath([])` — empty input\n- `expandPath([[0,1],[0,4]])` — two-segment path\n- `expandPath([[0,1],[0,4],[2,6]])` — three-segment path\n- `compressPath([])` — empty path (< 3 nodes, returns as-is)\n- `compressPath` — straight vertical then diagonal\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `interpolate` — horizontal line (`x0 != x1, y0 == y1`)\n- `interpolate` — diagonal line\n- `interpolate` — same start/end point (`x0==x1, y0==y1`) → single-element result\n- `backtrace` — no direct test; only exercised indirectly\n- `biBacktrace` — no direct test\n- `pathLength` — entirely untested; zero coverage\n- `smoothenPath` — entirely untested; the function also contains a **bug**: `lastValidCoord` is used without declaration (implicit global) at Util.js:167\n- `compressPath` with single-element path (length = 1) — boundary: returns path as-is\n- `compressPath` with two-element path (length = 2) — boundary\n\n**Priority:** High — `smoothenPath` has zero coverage AND contains an undeclared variable bug (`lastValidCoord` at line 167). `pathLength` and `biBacktrace` are completely untested.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/AStarFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios with default constructor (`DiagonalMovement.Never`, `manhattan` heuristic).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` + `octile`\n- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true, dontCrossCorners: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles`\n- Constructor with explicit `diagonalMovement` option (all four values)\n- Constructor with custom `heuristic` function\n- Constructor with `weight` != 1 (weighted A*)\n- No-path scenario (start/end isolated by walls) → should return `[]`\n- Start == End (same node) → should return `[[x,y]]` or `[]` — behavior unspecified/untested\n- `findPath` — neighbor already in open list with better g-score (the `openList.updateItem` branch at AStarFinder.js:116)\n\n**Priority:** High — the `weight`, custom heuristic, and no-path scenarios are critical behavioral paths with zero coverage.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/DijkstraFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (inherits AStarFinder with `heuristic = 0`).\n\n**What is NOT tested:** Same gaps as AStarFinder. Additionally:\n- Verify heuristic override to `0` — distances should reflect true uniform cost\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BestFirstFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal check only: start/end coords).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- Custom heuristic injection\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- Constructor option coverage (same as AStarFinder)\n- The `* 1000000` scaling effect: on an open grid, path should be greedy (go straight to goal)\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BreadthFirstFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios with default options.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- Diagonal movement enabled variants\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- Start == End\n- Constructor `allowDiagonal` / `dontCrossCorners` / `diagonalMovement` options\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BiAStarFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal check only).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- All constructor options (same as AStarFinder)\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- The `biBacktrace(node, neighbor)` meeting-point path join — only implicitly hit\n- The `biBacktrace(neighbor, node)` reverse direction join (end-side expansion finds start-side node)\n- Both expansion directions (start-side and end-side) meeting\n\n**Priority:** High — bi-directional meeting logic is complex and the two `biBacktrace` call sites are never explicitly asserted.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BiBreadthFirstFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (optimal check).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- Diagonal movement variants\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- `biBacktrace` call from end-side expansion (BiBreadthFirstFinder.js:100)\n- Start == End\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BiDijkstraFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (optimal).\n\n**What is NOT tested:** Same gaps as BiAStarFinder + DijkstraFinder.\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BiBestFirstFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal).\n\n**What is NOT tested:** Same gaps as BestFirstFinder + bi-directional meeting logic.\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/IDAStarFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal check only).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `trackRecursion: true` — `retainCount` and `tested` tracking branches (IDAStarFinder.js:137-144)\n- `timeLimit` option — path not found due to time expiry → `[]` (IDAStarFinder.js:105-108)\n- `weight` != 1\n- Custom heuristic\n- Diagonal movement variants\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- The `route` array construction (IDAStarFinder.js:118-121) — only implicitly verified\n\n**Priority:** High — `timeLimit` and `trackRecursion` are unique features with zero test coverage.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JumpPointFinder.js (factory)\n\n**What IS tested:**\n- `DiagonalMovement.Never` → `JPFNeverMoveDiagonally`\n- `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` → `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle`\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `DiagonalMovement.Always` → `JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally` — **no tests at all**\n- `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` → `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles` — **no tests at all**\n- Default (no option) → falls through to `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle`\n\n**Priority:** High — two of four factory branches (`Always`, `OnlyWhenNoObstacles`) produce untested finders.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Nothing — zero test coverage.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `_jump` — diagonal movement detection of forced neighbors (JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally.js:43-51)\n- `_jump` — horizontal forced neighbor detection (line 56-59)\n- `_jump` — vertical forced neighbor detection (line 61-64)\n- `_jump` — end-node detection\n- `_jump` — out-of-bounds / unwalkable returns null\n- `_findNeighbors` — diagonal parent direction (line 94-110)\n- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal parent direction\n- `_findNeighbors` — vertical parent direction\n- `_findNeighbors` — no parent (returns all neighbors)\n- End-to-end `findPath` — any maze at all\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n\n**Priority:** High — entire file untested.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Nothing — zero test coverage.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `_jump` — commented-out forced-neighbor check at line 44-47 (deliberate omission, but untested)\n- `_jump` — diagonal sub-jump calls (line 49)\n- `_jump` — horizontal forced neighbors (line 56-59)\n- `_jump` — vertical forced neighbors (line 62-65)\n- `_jump` — diagonal continuation gating (`isWalkableAt(x+dx,y) && isWalkableAt(x,y+dy)`) at line 75\n- `_findNeighbors` — all parent-direction branches\n- End-to-end `findPath` — any maze\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n\n**Priority:** High — entire file untested.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JPFNeverMoveDiagonally.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `_jump` — horizontal direction forced-neighbor detection (line 42-45)\n- `_jump` — vertical direction + recursive horizontal sub-jumps (line 53)\n- `_jump` — `throw new Error(\"Only horizontal and vertical movements are allowed\")` (line 58) — diagonal dx/dy input never tested\n- `_jump` — `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal parent direction\n- `_findNeighbors` — vertical parent direction\n- `_findNeighbors` — no parent\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n\n**Priority:** High — error-throw branch and recursion path in `_jump` uncovered.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `_jump` — diagonal forced-neighbor detection branches (line 43-47)\n- `_jump` — diagonal continuation gating (`isWalkableAt(x+dx,y) || isWalkableAt(x,y+dy)`) at line 71 — the `null` return branch when both blocked\n- `_jump` — `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n- `_findNeighbors` — diagonal parent: forced neighbor additions at lines 110-115\n- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal parent: forced-obstacle-adjacent diagonal neighbors\n- `_findNeighbors` — no parent\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n\n**Priority:** High — diagonal continuation null-return branch and forced-neighbor pruning logic untested.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JumpPointFinderBase.js\n\n**What IS tested:** `findPath` loop runs via all JPF subclass tests.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `_identifySuccessors` — `jumpNode.closed` skip branch (line 89)\n- `_identifySuccessors` — `openList.updateItem` branch (ng < jumpNode.g, line 107)\n- `trackJumpRecursion: true` option (base class stores flag but never tested at base level)\n- No-path scenario (open list exhausted) → `[]`\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## Cross-cutting gaps\n\n| Gap | Affected finders | Priority |\n|-----|-----------------|----------|\n| No-path (isolated start or end) returns `[]` | All 11 finders | **High** |\n| Start == End returns path | All finders | Medium |\n| `DiagonalMovement.Always` end-to-end | JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally | **High** |\n| `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` end-to-end | JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles | **High** |\n| `smoothenPath` — zero coverage + bug (undeclared `lastValidCoord`) | Util.js:167 | **High** |\n| `pathLength` — zero coverage | Util.js | **High** |\n| Heuristic unit tests | Heuristic.js | **High** |\n| `Grid.clone()` — zero direct coverage | Grid.js | High |\n| Matrix dimension mismatch error | Grid.js | Medium |\n| `IDAStarFinder` timeLimit expiry | IDAStarFinder.js | High |\n| `IDAStarFinder` trackRecursion | IDAStarFinder.js | Medium |\n| Deprecated `allowDiagonal` / `dontCrossCorners` options | AStarFinder, BFS, Dijkstra, … | Low |\n","numLines":347,"startLine":1,"totalLines":347}}}
