{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GHFkE2eCD7Pa9P7vunDQ2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to distribute work. Let me plan:\n\n**Coverage gaps (from gap-report.md):**\n\nHigh priority groups:\n1. Core utilities: Heuristic.js (unit tests), Util.js (smoothenPath, pathLength, biBacktrace, interpolate gaps)\n2. Grid.js: clone(), getNeighbors with Always/OnlyWhenNoObstacles, invalid diagonal, matrix mismatch, Node.js\n3. AStarFinder + DijkstraFinder + BestFirstFinder + BreadthFirstFinder (constructor options, no-path, start==end, weight)\n\n\n4. Bi-directional finders (BiAStarFinder, BiBreadthFirstFinder, BiDijkstraFinder, BiBestFirstFinder) need tests for meeting logic and no-path scenarios.\n5. IDAStarFinder requires coverage for timeLimit, trackRecursion, weight, custom heuristic, diagonal handling, and no-path cases.\n6. JumpPointFinder and its variants (JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally, JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles, JPFNeverMoveDiagonally, JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle, JumpPointFinderBase) are largely untested and need comprehensive coverage.\n\nNow I'm grouping these by effort and relatedness. Writer 1 should handle the core foundation modules—Heuristic, Util, Node, and DiagonalMovement—focusing on unit tests for all heuristic functions with edge cases, path utilities like smoothing and gap interpolation, and the diagonal movement enum. Writer 2 takes Grid.js and the standard pathfinding algorithms, covering Grid's neighbor retrieval logic, diagonal error handling, and the core finders like A*, Dijkstra, BestFirst, and BFS with their various options and edge cases.\n\nBut that's overloading Writer 2. Let me redistribute: Writer 1 stays with core utilities, Writer 2 handles Grid.js plus A* and Dijkstra, Writer 3 covers the bidirectional variants and IDA*, and Writer 4 takes all the JumpPoint implementations including the factory and base class. The bidirectional finders need to handle meeting logic, path reconstruction, and edge cases like no solution found. IDAStarFinder has high complexity with time limits and recursion tracking, while the JumpPoint variants are largely untested—especially the diagonal movement implementations. I'll also need to build out visual test scenarios based on the gaps document to validate everything works correctly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8080,"cache_read_input_tokens":14035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8080},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72a8c5be-b7cd-4258-8cfe-39ab16c21233","uuid":"ff0bf3b7-10f6-4930-abb6-434a45ee6263"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GHFkE2eCD7Pa9P7vunDQ2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading done. Now distributing work across writers.\n\n**Distribution plan:**\n- **Writer 1:** Core modules (Heuristic, Util, Node, DiagonalMovement)\n- **Writer 2:** Grid.js + AStarFinder + DijkstraFinder\n- **Writer 3:** BestFirst + BreadthFirst + all 4 Bi-directional finders\n- **Writer 4:** IDAStarFinder + all JumpPoint finders (factory + 4 variants + base)\n- **Scenario Builder:** Visual/UI test scenarios from visual audit"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8080,"cache_read_input_tokens":14035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8080},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72a8c5be-b7cd-4258-8cfe-39ab16c21233","uuid":"0bdb4ea5-4d8d-45fa-ade4-fd9df599472e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GHFkE2eCD7Pa9P7vunDQ2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TcHgRFk6ZdCm1Mw4mzVwFK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/test-writer-1/input/assignments.md","content":"# Test Writer 1 — Core Modules\n\n## Scope\nUnit tests for core utility modules: Heuristic.js, Util.js, Node.js, DiagonalMovement.js\n\n---\n\n## Priority 1 — src/core/Heuristic.js (HIGH)\n\nZero direct coverage. Pure functions, trivial to test but bugs here corrupt all finders.\n\n- `manhattan(dx, dy)` — e.g. `manhattan(3, 4)` → `7`\n- `euclidean(dx, dy)` — e.g. `euclidean(3, 4)` → `5`\n- `octile(dx, dy)` — both `dx < dy` and `dx >= dy` branches\n- `chebyshev(dx, dy)` — e.g. `chebyshev(3, 4)` → `4`\n- Zero inputs: all four with `(0, 0)` → `0`\n- Symmetry: `heuristic(a, b) === heuristic(b, a)` for octile and chebyshev\n\n## Priority 2 — src/core/Util.js (HIGH)\n\n- `smoothenPath` — entirely untested; also contains bug: `lastValidCoord` used without declaration (implicit global) at Util.js:167. Write tests that expose this.\n- `pathLength` — entirely untested; zero coverage\n- `biBacktrace` — no direct test; only exercised indirectly by bi-directional finders\n- `backtrace` — no direct test; only exercised indirectly\n- `interpolate` — horizontal line (`x0 != x1, y0 == y1`)\n- `interpolate` — diagonal line\n- `interpolate` — same start/end point (`x0==x1, y0==y1`) → single-element result\n- `compressPath` with single-element path (length = 1)\n- `compressPath` with two-element path (length = 2)\n\n## Priority 3 — src/core/Node.js (LOW)\n\n- Direct construction: `new Node(x, y)` — verify default `walkable=true`\n- Explicit `walkable=false` constructor arg\n\n## Priority 4 — src/core/DiagonalMovement.js (MEDIUM)\n\n- Verify enum values are stable: `Always=1`, `Never=2`, `IfAtMostOneObstacle=3`, `OnlyWhenNoObstacles=4`\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8080,"cache_read_input_tokens":14035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8080},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72a8c5be-b7cd-4258-8cfe-39ab16c21233","uuid":"f0b7aef8-a3bc-4f69-b27d-26a84e59eea9"}
