s (LOW)\n\n- Direct construction: `new Node(x, y)` — verify default `walkable=true`\n- Explicit `walkable=false` constructor arg\n\n## Priority 4 — src/core/DiagonalMovement.js (MEDIUM)\n\n- Verify enum values are stable: `Always=1`, `Never=2`, `IfAtMostOneObstacle=3`, `OnlyWhenNoObstacles=4`\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GHFkE2eCD7Pa9P7vunDQ2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FcyRqgTYLsBp3ydGu7V3J4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/test-writer-2/input/assignments.md","content":"# Test Writer 2 — Grid.js + AStarFinder + DijkstraFinder\n\n## Scope\nGrid core coverage gaps, AStarFinder constructor/edge-case coverage, DijkstraFinder verification.\n\n---\n\n## Priority 1 — src/core/Grid.js (HIGH)\n\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Always` — `d0=d1=d2=d3=true` branch (Grid.js:189)\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` — `d = s3 && s0` branch (Grid.js:180)\n- `getNeighbors` with invalid `diagonalMovement` → should throw `'Incorrect value of diagonalMovement'` (Grid.js:195)\n- `_buildNodes` with mismatched matrix dimensions → should throw `'Matrix size does not fit'` (Grid.js:66)\n- `clone()` — verify cloned grid has identical walkability; mutation of clone doesn't affect original\n- `getNodeAt` — direct test\n- Corner node neighbor pruning (nodes at grid edges where diagonal would be out-of-bounds)\n\n## Priority 2 — src/finders/AStarFinder.js (HIGH)\n\n- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` + `octile`\n- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true, dontCrossCorners: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles`\n- Constructor with explicit `diagonalMovement` option (all four values)\n- Constructor with custom `heuristic` function\n- Constructor with `weight` != 1 (weighted A*)\n- No-path scenario (start/end isolated by walls) → should return `[]`\n- Start == End (same node)\n- `findPath` — neighbor already in open list with better g-score (`openList.updateItem` branch at AStarFinder.js:116)\n\n## Priority 3 — src/finders/DijkstraFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n\n- Verify heuristic override to `0` — all neighbors explored uniformly\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- Constructor option passthrough\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8080,"cache_read_input_tokens":14035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8080},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72a8c5be-b7cd-4258-8cfe-39ab16c21233","uuid":"7d72b54c-d98b-43e2-af0f-2e5e9de52498"}
