king branches (IDAStarFinder.js:137-144)\n- `weight` != 1\n- Custom heuristic\n- Diagonal movement variants\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- The `route` array construction (IDAStarFinder.js:118-121)\n\n## Priority 4 — src/finders/JumpPointFinder.js factory (HIGH)\n\n- `DiagonalMovement.Always` → `JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally` — verify correct class selected\n- `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` → `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles` — verify correct class\n- Default (no option) → falls through to `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle`\n\n## Priority 5 — src/finders/JPFNeverMoveDiagonally.js (HIGH)\n\n- `_jump` — horizontal forced-neighbor detection (line 42-45)\n- `_jump` — vertical + recursive horizontal sub-jumps (line 53)\n- `_jump` — `throw new Error(\"Only horizontal and vertical movements are allowed\")` (line 58)\n- `_jump` — `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal, vertical, no parent\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n\n## Priority 6 — src/finders/JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle.js (HIGH)\n\n- `_jump` — diagonal forced-neighbor detection (line 43-47)\n- `_jump` — diagonal continuation gating null-return when both blocked (line 71)\n- `_jump` — `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n- `_findNeighbors` — diagonal parent forced-neighbor additions (lines 110-115)\n- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal parent forced-obstacle-adjacent diagonal neighbors\n- `_findNeighbors` — no parent\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n\n## Priority 7 — src/finders/JumpPointFinderBase.js (MEDIUM)\n\n- `_identifySuccessors` — `jumpNode.closed` skip branch (line 89)\n- `_identifySuccessors` — `openList.updateItem` branch (ng < jumpNode.g, line 107)\n- `trackJumpRecursion: true` option\n- No-path scenario (open list exhausted) → `[]`\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GHFkE2eCD7Pa9P7vunDQ2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017EJ7WbfH7nJtWp6Z2r5PzN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/scenario-builder/input/assignments.md","content":"# Scenario Builder — Visual & UI Test Scenarios\n\n## Scope\nBuild test scenarios for the visual demo app based on gaps identified in the visual audit.\n\n---\n\n## Priority 1 — Bug: IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\n\n**File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\n**Bug:** Reads `input[name=jump_point_heuristic]` instead of `input[name=ida_heuristic]`\n**Scenario:** Select IDA*, pick Euclidean in IDA* panel, run search. Verify heuristic actually used matches selection, not JPS panel.\n\n## Priority 2 — No \"path not found\" feedback\n\n**File:** `visual/js/view.js:245`\n**Scenario:** Surround start node with walls. Run any algorithm. Verify user gets clear \"No path found\" message instead of silent finish with `length: 0`.\n\n## Priority 3 — Start equals end\n\n**Scenario:** Drag end node onto start node position. Run search. Verify no crash, graceful zero-length path or no-op.\n\n## Priority 4 — Drag start/end during search\n\n**Scenario:** Begin search, attempt to drag start/end while animating. Verify state machine blocks drag (only allowed in `ready`/`finished` states). No crash or state corruption.\n\n## Priority 5 — Wall on start or end position\n\n**Scenario:** Place wall on start node position. Run search. Expect graceful failure, not crash.\n\n## Priority 6 — Pause / Resume cycle\n\n**Scenario:** Start search, pause mid-animation, resume. Verify animation continues from exact paused state with no duplicate or skipped operations.\n\n## Priority 7 — Restart during search\n\n**Scenario:** Start search, click Restart before finish. Verify animation clears, new search begins cleanly, no stale colored nodes remain.\n\n## Priority 8 — JPS diagonal modes not selectable\n\n**Gap:** Only 2 of 4 JumpPointFinder diagonal modes exposed in UI. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` missing.\n**Scenario:** Document what UI changes needed; build scenario that exercises all 4 modes if dropdown were added.\n\n## Priority 9 — Bi-directional vs unidirectional comparison\n\n**Scenario:** Same grid, run A* unidirectional then bi-directional. Verify bi-directional explores fewer nodes; same or similar path.\n\n## Priority 10 — Weight parameter effect\n\n**Scenario:** Run A* with weight=1 vs weight=5 on same grid. Higher weight → fewer operations (greedier) but potentially longer path.\n\n## Priority 11 — IDA* time limit\n\n**Scenario:** Dense wall grid, set time limit to 1ms, run IDA*. Verify IDA* aborts at time limit with some feedback.\n\n## Priority 12 — Full grid walls\n\n**Scenario:** Draw walls everywhere. Run search. Verify robust no-path handling, no JS errors.\n\n## Priority 13 — Large operation count performance\n\n**Scenario:** Dijkstra or BFS on open 64x36 grid, start top-left, end bottom-right. Verify animation remains smooth at 300 ops/sec.\n\n## Priority 14 — Adjacent start/end\n\n**Scenario:** Start and end nodes 1 step apart. Verify minimal animation, path length ~1, fast finish.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8080,"cache_read_input_tokens":14035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8080},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72a8c5be-b7cd-4258-8cfe-39ab16c21233","uuid":"41b46cae-a9e0-4008-b732-49c28c49a60d"}
