{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01N7HUM467cN8WJ2B1GqjSZ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RNGpQVToqQE6Sy7jaffE68","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/orchestrator/output/distribution-plan.md","content":"# Orchestrator Distribution Plan\n\n**Date:** 2026-04-16  \n**Inputs:** coverage-auditor/gap-report.md, visual-auditor/visual-gaps.md\n\n---\n\n## Distribution\n\n| Worker | Scope | Est. Effort | Gap Count |\n|--------|-------|-------------|-----------|\n| test-writer-1 | Core modules: Heuristic.js, Util.js, Node.js, DiagonalMovement.js | High | ~20 gaps |\n| test-writer-2 | Grid.js + AStarFinder + DijkstraFinder | High | ~18 gaps |\n| test-writer-3 | BestFirst + BreadthFirst + 4 Bi-directional finders | Medium-High | ~18 gaps |\n| test-writer-4 | IDAStarFinder + JumpPointFinder factory + 4 JPF variants + JPF base | High | ~30 gaps |\n| scenario-builder | Visual/UI test scenarios from visual audit | Medium | 14 scenarios |\n\n## Grouping rationale\n\n- **Writer 1** gets all pure-function core utilities. Heuristic + Util gaps are high-priority, self-contained, no finder dependencies. Includes the `smoothenPath` bug (undeclared `lastValidCoord`).\n- **Writer 2** gets Grid (foundational) + AStarFinder (base class for many finders) + DijkstraFinder (thin wrapper). Related: Grid neighbor logic feeds directly into A* pathfinding.\n- **Writer 3** gets remaining standard finders + all bi-directional variants. Bi-finders share meeting-point logic (`biBacktrace`), so grouping them avoids duplicate test infrastructure.\n- **Writer 4** gets IDA* (unique features: timeLimit, trackRecursion) + entire JumpPoint family (2 entirely untested files, complex jump/neighbor logic). Heaviest assignment but all JPF variants share structure — test patterns reusable across variants.\n- **Scenario builder** gets all visual/UI gaps: bugs (IDA* heuristic), missing feedback (no-path), interaction edge cases (drag during search, pause/resume), and missing UI features.\n\n## Cross-cutting: no-path scenario\n\nAll 11 finders need no-path tests. Distributed as follows:\n- Writer 2: AStar, Dijkstra\n- Writer 3: BestFirst, BreadthFirst, BiAStar, BiBreadthFirst, BiDijkstra, BiBestFirst\n- Writer 4: IDAStar, all JPF variants\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5768,"cache_read_input_tokens":22115,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5768},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72a8c5be-b7cd-4258-8cfe-39ab16c21233","uuid":"ac3bac07-9911-4732-8753-5031136804b7"}
